KG42.register("rules-bf30366d04e230da1d4046ad",{"id":"19-two_stage_battery_sharing::v141-c-R006","paper":"19-two_stage_battery_sharing","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R006","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local energy product","process_stage":"bidding","market_meaning":"Surplus PV electricity may be shared between prosumers and traded with consumers without PV systems. Scope: P2P energy sharing within the community Microgrid. Condition: Surplus PV power is available. Total selling power comes from PV battery systems and equals the remaining PV power after charging or discharging activities; total buying power is customer demand. Scope: Definition of selling and buying power for community Microgrid P2P energy sharing.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function product.local_energy under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["product.local_energy"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Definition of selling and buying power for community Microgrid P2P energy sharing. | P2P energy sharing within the community Microgrid.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e007","v141-b-g02-E19"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Surplus PV electricity may be shared between prosumers and traded with consumers without PV systems. Scope: P2P energy sharing within the community Microgrid. Condition: Surplus PV power is available.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e007"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Total selling power comes from PV battery systems and equals the remaining PV power after charging or discharging activities; total buying power is customer demand. Scope: Definition of selling and buying power for community Microgrid P2P energy sharing.","expression":"\\text{total selling power at }t=\\sum_{i=1}^{NB}\\left(P_{PV,t}^{i}-P_{aggBC,t}^{i}+P_{aggBD,t}^{i}\\right);\\quad \\text{total buying power at }t=\\sum_{i=1}^{N}P_{L,t}^{i}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E19"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e007","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":4,"printed_page":"264","section":"2.1. P2P energy sharing structure","anchor_text":"g p g time when there is insuﬃcient energy from the PV battery system, the prosumer buys energy from","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 1","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"P2P energy sharing provides options for prosumers to trade energy within the neighborhood through local buying and selling, allowing local funds to remain within the local economy [31]. With P2P energy sharing, several customers in a community Microgrid share the connection to the main grid. The combined load is subject to random coincidence of the individual loads, which averages stochastic fluctuations [32,33]. This means that surplus PV power from a customer can be consumed by another customer with excess consumption.\nFig. 1 shows the architecture of P2P energy sharing. In the P2P sharing community, there are N customers, NB of which have individual PV battery systems installed (NB ⩽ N). Although the PV outputs in a community are likely to be similar due to almost the same solar radiation, the net loads vary between prosumers, because of the differences in load, kWp of PV systems and battery statuses. Therefore, it is possible for the prosumers to share PV power with each other. The surplus PV power from prosumers can also be traded with consumers who do not have PV systems."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E19","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"3.3. P2P trading mechanism Given the fact that in economics the relation between price and SDR is in","equation_id":"(17)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Given the fact that in economics the relation between price and SDR is inverse-proportional, reference [13] formulated a P2P pricing model based on the supply and demand ratio. Here, the SDR method is also used. The total selling power is from the PV battery systems, which is equal to the remaining PV power after carrying out the charging or discharging activities, and the total buying power is the customer demand. Thus, the SDR at a community Microgrid at time t is defined as, SDR^{t} = \\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^{NB} (P_{PV,t}^{i} - P_{aggBC,t}^{i} + P_{aggBD,t}^{i})}{\\sum_{i=1}^{N} P_{L,t}^{i}} \\quad (17)"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"No design-selection or operational-decision variable is introduced in this rule. The source defines aggregate selling and buying power from time-indexed PV, battery and load quantities whose decision roles are defined elsewhere; declaring them as x here would misstate their optimization role.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed parameter or constant is introduced in this rule. The aggregate identity uses time-indexed power quantities whose parameter/variable roles are not assigned by the frozen graph for this rule."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"product.local_energy","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e007","quote":"Therefore, it is possible for the prosumers to share PV power with each other. The surplus PV power from prosumers can also be traded with consumers who do not have PV systems."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E19","quote":"The total selling power is from the PV battery systems, which is equal to the remaining PV power after carrying out the charging or discharging activities, and the total buying power is the customer demand."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"605dc6b75d6e8c1536a93507c64011a3e693e766d57d13746828491ef95245d4","applicability":"formalized","reason":"Partial source-grounded formalization: C001 remains procedural because the supplied source describes surplus-PV sharing/trading eligibility rather than a mathematical relation. C002 is formalized from the numerator and denominator of Eq. (17), which define total selling power as the remaining PV power after battery charging/discharging and total buying power as customer demand. The SDR ratio itself is a pricing construct and is not asserted here as part of the local energy product. B evidence, including v141-b-g02-E19, remains unreviewed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","node_ids":["product.local_energy"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C001 states the procedural scope and condition under which surplus PV electricity is the local energy product shared or traded within the community Microgrid. The frozen rule contains only the product.local_energy node and no edge."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C002","node_ids":["product.local_energy"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C002 defines the aggregate selling and buying quantities constituting the local energy product. The source expression is transcribed from the numerator and denominator of Eq. (17); the frozen graph has no edge for this unary product definition."}],"revision_requests":["Confirm whether Eq. (17)'s SDR ratio belongs to the pricing rule v141-c-R005 or should remain only as context within v141-c-R006; this patch formalizes only the selling-power and buying-power numerator/denominator, not the SDR ratio itself.","If P_{PV,t}^{i}, P_{aggBC,t}^{i}, P_{aggBD,t}^{i} and P_{L,t}^{i} are to be objectified in this rule, C.1 should provide their typed x/theta roles and scopes; they are intentionally not re-declared here to avoid cross-rule reuse."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
